WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:03.180
- [Man] T-minus 10, nine, eight, seven,

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:04.850
six, five, four, three.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:07.103
- There's a border that all of us share.

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:11.313
And it keeps getting closer and closer.

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:13.993
It's right above our heads.

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:18.470
But it's not a border
between two countries,

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:20.370
it's actually a boundary to a place

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:23.203
that used to be accessible
to just a few of us,

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:27.950
but now more and more of
us can cross this boundary.

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:30.900
- [Reporter] What's been dubbed
the billionaire space race.

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:35.260
- And as that happens,

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:37.940
we humans risk messing it up.

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:40.440
We risk sealing this border completely

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.530
so no person or object can escape earth.

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:45.930
I want to show you how this might happen

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:48.300
and what we can do to avoid it.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.550
- [Woman] Long-term simulations

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:51.010
show an exponential growth

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:53.370
in the number of objects in space.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:55.303
- This is low earth orbit.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:02.260
It's a zone about a thousand
kilometers above earth.

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:03.660
This is a place where earth's gravity

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:05.300
can kind of pull you down,

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:08.740
but just enough to put you
into a perpetual free fall

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:10.660
that we call an orbit.

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:12.030
Satellites we send into space

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:13.940
can orbit earth as far out

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.290
as tens of thousands of kilometers,

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:18.490
but it is in this low earth orbit

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:21.270
where a majority of
earth's satellites reside.

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:24.870
The satellites here give
us images like these

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:27.480
from telescopes like this.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:30.230
They also allow us to
anticipate hurricanes,

00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:32.970
and observe trends like these.

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:35.380
These satellites gave
us the satellite phone.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:36.750
- Who has the satellite phone?

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:38.670
- They connect people to the internet,

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:40.860
and they help us map the world,

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:43.590
which is something I am very grateful for.

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:47.337
The satellites in low earth
orbit are incredibly important.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:51.730
Okay so how many satellites are up there?

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:54.110
Like 50 or maybe 100?

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:58.443
Let's see, how many, I'm Googling
on my phone, let's check.

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:01.830
6,000?

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:03.530
6,000?

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:05.871
Whoa, okay.

00:02:05.871 --> 00:02:09.250
So there's 6,000 satellites
floating around the earth.

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:11.110
Turns out that half of those are dead.

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:12.230
They used to be satellites,

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:14.470
now they're just hunks of metal

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:18.740
the size of a small school bus
spinning around our planet.

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:21.260
Of the 3,000 or so working satellites,

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:24.610
some are military, some are government,

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:28.070
but more than half of them are commercial.

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:29.360
Sorry, did that land?

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:30.590
Let me just say it again.

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:33.630
Half of the satellites are commercial,

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:35.683
they're from private companies.

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:39.240
Let me explain why that's a big deal.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:41.970
For most of the time that
we've been traveling to space,

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:44.110
space has been a government thing.

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:45.980
It was Russia that put
up the first satellite

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:47.990
into low earth orbit in the '50s.

00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:51.780
It was the Cold War so the U.S.
was like we can do that too,

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:52.950
and we're gonna do it better,

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:55.300
so they created NASA, and focused

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.790
on getting as many
satellites as they could

00:02:57.790 --> 00:02:58.890
up into space.

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:00.890
- We need science,

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:02.760
this is for the American people,

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:04.680
the most critical problem of all.

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:06.690
- A bunch of these launches
just sort of blew up

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:08.430
because they were really terribly made,

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:10.840
but eventually they got
satellites into space.

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:12.490
They had something to prove.

00:03:12.490 --> 00:03:14.600
Space was a political thing at the time.

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:17.090
- President Eisenhower
reassures the nation

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:19.780
that Russia's success
with the first satellite

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:23.480
does not indicate a serious lag
in American rocket research.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:27.010
- And the U.S. poured tons of
money into making this happen,

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:28.090
and they did.

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:30.410
- Our satellite is definitely on orbit.

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:33.750
- So at this point space
was a government thing,

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:36.316
but boy has that changed.

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:38.899
(upbeat music)

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:43.150
In recent years there
has been an explosion

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:45.260
of satellites being put into space

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:47.550
that are not from the
government or military,

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:49.480
but from private businesses,

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:51.330
to the point where today in 2021

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.770
there are over 100 private companies

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:58.330
that are building vehicles to
take more stuff into space.

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:01.030
This is a space economy, it's a big deal.

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:02.930
And because of that, more and more stuff

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:04.730
is going into space.

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:07.530
This year, 2021, we've already launched

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:10.020
1100 objects into space.

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:13.420
That's the same total as
we did in all of 2020,

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:16.920
and nearly 10% of what we've
ever sent up into space.

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:20.700
The numbers are going up
faster and faster and faster

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:22.360
every single year.

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:26.150
But there's a problem,
potentially a huge problem

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:29.460
with all of this stuff
going up into space,

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:33.650
and that problem is that space,
at least low earth orbit,

00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:37.440
this area right around
our earth is limited.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:39.760
Let me explain what I mean here.

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:43.010
You have all of these objects
floating around our earth.

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:45.370
More and more every year.

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:48.290
So what happens if two of these satellites

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:50.253
by chance collide?

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:54.150
So what?

00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:55.410
Satellites collide and maybe

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:59.390
some rich company loses
some money, who cares?

00:04:59.390 --> 00:05:03.330
No, no no no no no, no no no no.

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:05.820
Reminder that these objects
are flying around earth

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:09.400
at 28,000 kilometers an hour,

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.850
that's eight kilometers a second.

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:14.210
That's one second, eight kilometers.

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:16.770
They go around earth 12 times per day.

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:19.570
And at that speed, things
get a little bit crazy.

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:21.900
A few years ago, a fleck of debris,

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:23.310
like a little piece of dust

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:25.230
that was one millimeter in diameter,

00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:28.540
like the tip of a sharp
pencil, a tiny fleck,

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:31.550
was floating through low
earth orbit at this speed,

00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:34.040
and it hit a satellite's solar panels.

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:35.610
And this tiny fleck of dust

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:38.660
left a giant gash in the panels.

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:40.750
It was one millimeter in diameter.

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:45.360
In 2009, a collision between
a defunct Russian space craft

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:48.160
and an operational commercial satellite

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:51.780
created this exact kind of shrapnel cloud,

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:53.370
completely disintegrated.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:56.400
More than 2,300 hunks of space junk

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:58.740
that are now floating around our planet

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:02.040
at 28,000 kilometers an hour.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:05.330
This shrapnel at one point put
the Hubble Telescope at risk,

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:07.150
and it sort of freaked people out.

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:11.960
In an instant, two objects
turned into thousands of objects,

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:14.830
all with new paths
floating around our earth.

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:16.600
So the fear here is that

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.320
what if this became a chain reaction?

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:20.690
One collision makes more debris

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:22.920
which leads to another collision

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:26.000
which means even more
debris, and more collisions,

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:27.870
and suddenly low earth orbit

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:30.700
becomes a minefield of space junk

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:33.700
hurling around our
planet at deathly speeds

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:35.250
and launches a domino effect

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:37.960
that would wipe out our
space infrastructure

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:40.450
leaving us trapped on the surface of earth

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:43.600
for generations beneath a violent cloud

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:45.210
of speeding shrapnel.

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:48.823
Unable to send anything up to
space for a very long time.

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:53.200
This is the nightmare scenario.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:56.750
It's a scenario that's
portrayed in the movie Gravity

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:58.533
which is a very good movie.

