00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:20.700
All right, let's get
back to space borders.

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:22.810
Eventually of course, over the years,

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:25.940
this debris would slowly
fall into the atmosphere,

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:26.773
it would lose altitude,

00:08:26.773 --> 00:08:28.990
and it would burn up in our atmosphere.

00:08:28.990 --> 00:08:33.150
But that would be generations
of a world without satellites.

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:35.600
A world that is sealed from space.

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:36.690
Okay okay listen listen,

00:08:36.690 --> 00:08:38.900
this is not gonna happen anytime soon,

00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:41.820
by all counts we are safe
from the chain reaction,

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:43.430
the probabilities are very low.

00:08:43.430 --> 00:08:44.650
It isn't likely right now.

00:08:44.650 --> 00:08:46.020
There's a lot of space up there.

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:49.020
- [Man] Space, the final frontier.

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:50.210
- But we are sending up

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:52.860
thousands of satellites per year now.

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:54.540
This may not be an issue now,

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:56.130
it certainly will be soon.

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:57.940
So what do you do with this?

00:08:57.940 --> 00:09:00.470
We're in the midst of this new space race,

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:02.010
just like the one between the Soviets

00:09:02.010 --> 00:09:03.440
and the U.S. in the '50s

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:05.780
but this time it's not governments,

00:09:05.780 --> 00:09:07.480
it's like this guy,

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:09.657
and a bunch of guys just like him.

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:14.100
And they're the ones
who are racing to space,

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:15.740
and they don't really care about

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:18.570
the potential scenario
of a chain reaction.

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:19.480
Do you know why?

00:09:19.480 --> 00:09:21.390
Because they have investors to please,

00:09:21.390 --> 00:09:23.260
and a world to show that they can

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:26.031
privatize space the fastest.

00:09:26.031 --> 00:09:27.210
(laughing)

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:29.970
So let's talk about the U.S.
government really quick.

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:31.998
Of the 3,000 working satellites,

00:09:31.998 --> 00:09:35.100
about 2,000 of them are American.

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:36.390
They come from American companies

00:09:36.390 --> 00:09:37.670
or the American government.

00:09:37.670 --> 00:09:41.310
So you would expect the American
space government agency,

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:44.210
NASA, to be the responsible steward

00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:45.750
of low earth orbit,

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:47.830
and make sure that these
private space companies

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:50.110
are at least following some traffic rules

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:51.930
when they send them up into space

00:09:51.930 --> 00:09:53.260
so that they don't collide.

00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:56.340
Alas, no one, including NASA,

00:09:56.340 --> 00:10:00.050
wants to be the one to slow
down the new space race.

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:02.470
Instead they are focusing on quote,

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:05.620
accelerating a thriving commercial economy

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:07.040
in low earth orbit.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.510
The U.S. government is sort of doing

00:10:08.510 --> 00:10:10.030
what it did in the '50s,

00:10:10.030 --> 00:10:12.400
we've got a get an edge
on this new space thing

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:14.080
and let's focus on just getting

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:15.960
as much stuff up as we can.

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:19.210
So NASA is helping to fund
these private space companies

00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:21.770
who are sending up so many satellites

00:10:21.770 --> 00:10:23.340
and objects into space.

00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:25.640
Like SpaceX, Elon Musk's company

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:29.143
is sending up 60 satellites a month.

00:10:30.110 --> 00:10:33.880
60 satellites just being
thrust into space every month,

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:35.390
and he's asked for a lot more.

00:10:35.390 --> 00:10:38.360
He wants to get 42,000 up there.

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:40.310
That's what he's asking for,

00:10:40.310 --> 00:10:41.800
that's what he's asking for approval for,

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:45.250
42,000, just 42,000.

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:48.110
So far he's gotten approval for 12,000.

00:10:48.110 --> 00:10:50.470
Amazon is now getting into the space game.

00:10:50.470 --> 00:10:53.390
They've been approved
to send up over 3,000.

00:10:53.390 --> 00:10:54.960
We're not slowing down.

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:56.990
So clearly the race is on,

00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:59.830
and no one's thinking
too hard about traffic.

00:10:59.830 --> 00:11:01.800
- You're blaming me for the traffic?

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:02.633
- Should I?

00:11:02.633 --> 00:11:06.000
- So how do we avoid
filling up low earth orbit?

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:07.370
And avoid the collisions

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:09.060
that could potentially cause

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:10.800
a devastating chain reaction.

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:12.810
These companies are taking some protocol,

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:14.900
like SpaceX will send up these satellites

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:15.960
in like a caravan,

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:17.970
like a line of satellites

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:19.550
which looks really trippy by the way.

00:11:19.550 --> 00:11:23.160
I was out stargazing for
my galaxy video last year

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:27.000
and I looked up and I saw
this like perfect line

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:29.950
of blinking dots in the sky

00:11:29.950 --> 00:11:32.103
and I was like what is happening?

00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:35.310
I was sure that I was seeing a UFO,

00:11:35.310 --> 00:11:37.073
like this is it.

00:11:37.073 --> 00:11:41.630
Like I've had my encounter
with extra terrestrials.

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:42.970
It was like an existential moment for me,

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:44.760
I was like what is happening?

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:46.390
20 minutes later I looked it up

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:50.803
and learned about the
caravans that SpaceX does.

00:11:52.370 --> 00:11:54.530
They do this so that all of the satellites

00:11:54.530 --> 00:11:55.830
are in the same path

00:11:55.830 --> 00:11:58.630
so that they have way less
likelihood of colliding

00:11:58.630 --> 00:11:59.950
because they're not just on random paths

00:11:59.950 --> 00:12:00.950
they're like all together.

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:02.060
So yeah these private companies

00:12:02.060 --> 00:12:03.530
are taking some precautions,

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:04.480
but as we all know,

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:06.610
you can't rely on private companies

00:12:06.610 --> 00:12:09.170
to regulate themselves
for the good of everyone.

00:12:09.170 --> 00:12:11.110
Like, are we really gonna be like

00:12:12.432 --> 00:12:13.370
you guys regulate yourself

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:16.369
and we'll all be safe and
everyone will be good, no.

00:12:16.369 --> 00:12:18.150
That's not how it works.

00:12:18.150 --> 00:12:21.190
What we need is mutually agreed upon laws

00:12:21.190 --> 00:12:24.630
on how stuff can be launched
into low earth orbit

00:12:24.630 --> 00:12:28.490
so that we actually have some
traffic management in space.

00:12:28.490 --> 00:12:32.300
There are no rules of the road in space,

00:12:32.300 --> 00:12:35.490
no formal agreements on
how traffic should behave

00:12:35.490 --> 00:12:36.870
in low earth orbit.

00:12:36.870 --> 00:12:39.783
In other words, this is the wild west.

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:43.240
Wait, isn't there like space law?

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:44.530
Like treaties?

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:47.610
Like the outer space
treaty, the moon treaty,

00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:49.140
the International Space Station,

00:12:49.140 --> 00:12:51.840
yeah but none of these
things talk about traffic.

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:53.580
All these countries have
signed these treaties

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:55.890
that just say space is for everybody,

00:12:55.890 --> 00:12:58.750
no one can conquer space, no Star Wars.

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:00.240
- That isn't very reassuring.

00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:02.310
- Closest any treaty gets to addressing

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:03.760
the space traffic thing,

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:06.570
says that quote, states shall be liable

00:13:06.570 --> 00:13:09.950
for damage caused by their space objects.

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:12.370
In other words, if you send an object up,

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:15.480
and your country damages an
object from another country,

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:18.580
your country has to take
responsibility in some form.

00:13:18.580 --> 00:13:20.880
But wait, does that actually happen?

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:23.100
Remember that defunct Russian space craft

00:13:23.100 --> 00:13:26.200
that collided with the
commercial satellite in 2009?

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:28.050
Who took responsibility?

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:29.840
And wait, was it the Russian satellite

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:31.580
that hit the commercial one,

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:34.630
or was it the commercial one
that hit the Russian one?

00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:36.640
Like how do you dole out responsibility

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:39.427
and blame when you're talking about

00:13:39.427 --> 00:13:41.280
two satellites just floating through space

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:42.870
who happen to run into each other.

00:13:42.870 --> 00:13:44.730
So in the end, the responsibility

00:13:44.730 --> 00:13:48.780
landed squarely on the
shoulders of, nobody.

00:13:48.780 --> 00:13:50.420
- How did we get into this mess?

00:13:50.420 --> 00:13:51.980
- Decision makers couldn't even agree

00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:53.360
on who was responsible

00:13:53.360 --> 00:13:55.770
for launching the commercial
satellite in the first place

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:59.330
because multiple countries were
involved with launching it,

00:13:59.330 --> 00:14:01.270
and they hadn't registered it with the UN

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:04.860
like they promised they would
back in some treaty in 1972.

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:07.010
I mean it's a total mess.

00:14:07.010 --> 00:14:12.010
There is no order or regulation
or clarity in space law,

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:15.440
which right now is fine,
but soon it won't be.

00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:17.980
So here we are with no traffic rules,

00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:20.370
no history of holding anyone accountable

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:22.440
for unintentional space collisions,

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:23.720
and we're about to send up

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:26.060
tens of thousands more satellites.

00:14:26.060 --> 00:14:29.300
What we need is productive cooperation,

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:30.660
like humans have been able to do

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:34.070
in so many aspects of our
global international system.

00:14:34.070 --> 00:14:36.580
The International Space
Station is a great example.

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:37.800
It has functioned

00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:41.330
as a multi-national
collaborative project in space.

00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:43.520
Unfortunately what I've learned

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:46.600
is that when there's
competition among countries,

00:14:46.600 --> 00:14:49.200
a lot of these cooperative efforts

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.990
sort of go out the window.

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:54.100
There is growing tension
between two super powers,

00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:55.870
China and the U.S.

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:57.370
And China is in the middle of constructing

00:14:57.370 --> 00:15:00.350
their own space station
for low earth orbit.

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:03.670
India is preparing to
send their own as well.

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:06.180
This is competition, not cooperation.

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:08.210
Our existing space law,

00:15:08.210 --> 00:15:11.360
which was all sort of drafted
in the '60s and the '70s

00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:13.960
never anticipated private companies

00:15:13.960 --> 00:15:16.910
sending up thousands of satellites.

00:15:16.910 --> 00:15:20.640
And it didn't anticipate
China and India and the U.S.

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:23.900
Competing for space power.

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:25.950
Our desire to explore space

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:28.880
is not just about showing how powerful

00:15:28.880 --> 00:15:30.780
and innovative we are.

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:35.290
So much technology has come
from our space exploration.

00:15:35.290 --> 00:15:38.900
From solar cells to cochlear implants,

00:15:38.900 --> 00:15:40.970
to firefighting technology.

00:15:40.970 --> 00:15:42.720
The development of the micro chip

00:15:42.720 --> 00:15:45.360
which was majorly accelerated by NASA,

00:15:45.360 --> 00:15:47.960
and now microchips drive our entire world.

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:50.290
The pursuit of reaching out into space

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:54.010
has consistently driven
meaningful innovation.

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:55.580
So this is important,

00:15:55.580 --> 00:15:58.490
we should absolutely protect the future

00:15:58.490 --> 00:16:02.090
of this really wonderful
thing that humans have done.

00:16:02.090 --> 00:16:03.840
We've escaped our atmosphere,

00:16:03.840 --> 00:16:05.680
we've escaped gravity,

00:16:05.680 --> 00:16:07.740
and we've learned so much in the process.

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:11.370
So, there are a lot of objects in space,

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:12.573
they're floating around,

00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:16.580
and there is a body of treaties and law

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:18.590
that is way outdated.

00:16:18.590 --> 00:16:21.930
My hope is that as we send
these thousands and thousands

00:16:21.930 --> 00:16:24.580
of satellites into space,

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:27.060
we consider the
implications of what happens

00:16:27.060 --> 00:16:30.110
if we get too hasty,
send too much stuff up

00:16:30.110 --> 00:16:32.050
and things start to run into each other.

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:34.010
It's not worth the risk in my mind.

00:16:34.010 --> 00:16:35.210
If we don't look ahead,

00:16:35.210 --> 00:16:37.590
we could turn space from a border

00:16:37.590 --> 00:16:39.750
that we can all cross together,

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:41.640
and learn together as human beings,

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:44.120
into a border that is impenetrable,

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:46.758
that's dangerous, that keeps us trapped

00:16:46.758 --> 00:16:49.630
here on this warming planet,

00:16:49.630 --> 00:16:54.630
unable to continue to explore
the world of outer space.

00:16:54.769 --> 00:16:57.186
(soft music)

